.Dd September 19, 2026
.Dt NULL 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm null ,
.Nm zero ,
.Nm full
.Nd empty devices
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Pa /dev/null
.Pp
.Pa /dev/zero
.Pp
.Pa /dev/full
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These devices are provided by the kernel's devfs file system, mounted at
.Pa /dev .
.Pp
Reads from
.Pa /dev/null
return end of file.
Writes are discarded.
.Pp
Reads from
.Pa /dev/zero
return bytes with value zero, without end.
.Pp
Reads from
.Pa /dev/full
return bytes with value zero.
Writes fail with
.Er ENOSPC .
.Sh FILES
All three devices have mode 0666.
Their major and minor numbers, as reported by
.Xr stat 2 ,
are:
.Bl -tag -width /dev/zero
.It Pa /dev/null
Major 1, minor 3.
.It Pa /dev/zero
Major 1, minor 5.
.It Pa /dev/full
Major 1, minor 7.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bootlog 4 ,
.Xr console 4 ,
.Xr disk 4 ,
.Xr loop 4 ,
.Xr random 4
